# Refactored to Async/Await

Here are two approaches to refactor this function:

## Option 1: Using Promisify (Recommended)

```javascript
const util = require('util');

// Promisify the db.query method once
const queryAsync = util.promisify(db.query).bind(db);

async function getUser(id) {
  const rows = await queryAsync('SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ?', [id]);

  if (!rows.length) {
    throw new Error('Not found');
  }

  return rows[0];
}
```

## Option 2: Manual Promise Wrapper

```javascript
async function getUser(id) {
  const rows = await new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    db.query('SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ?', [id], (err, rows) => {
      if (err) return reject(err);
      resolve(rows);
    });
  });

  if (!rows.length) {
    throw new Error('Not found');
  }

  return rows[0];
}
```

## Usage Example

```javascript
// Old callback style
getUser(123, (err, user) => {
  if (err) console.error(err);
  else console.log(user);
});

// New async/await style
try {
  const user = await getUser(123);
  console.log(user);
} catch (err) {
  console.error(err);
}
```

**Key changes:**
- Removed the `callback` parameter
- Errors are now thrown instead of passed to callback
- Success values are returned directly
- Function is marked as `async`

